  1. Internal package imports rewritten from `doubao_murmur.xxx` to
     `doubao_input.doubao.xxx`.
  2. Resource path lookups (`_load_js_resource`) rewritten to read from
     `../login/resources/` instead of `importlib.resources`.
  3. `audio_capture.py`: added an `on_rms` callback hook (int16 RMS
     computed in the audio thread) to drive a real-time waveform in the
     overlay. Upstream only sent raw PCM downstream.
  4. `transcription.py`: added `handle_press()` / `handle_release()`
     methods and a 150 ms debounce (`MIN_PRESS_DURATION`) on top of the
     upstream `handle_toggle()` API, converting the toggle interaction
     into a push-to-hold (push-to-talk) interaction.
  5. `login_window.py`: window title changed from "Doubao Murmur - 登录"
     to "登录豆包" (plus the app icon), so the upstream project name is not
     leaked into this app's UI.

Everything else under `src/doubao_input/` (trigger/, inject/, ui/, hud/,
app.py, __main__.py) is original work for this project.

Tests under `tests/probe/` are original work.

## Desktop user interface: Myna (Canonical Ltd.)

The desktop presentation layer is modelled on / wired to
**Myna** (https://github.com/canonical/myna), which is licensed under the
**GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 or later** — the same licence as
this project.

### Vendored renderer: `vendor/`

`vendor/myna-hud/`, `vendor/myna-platform/` and `vendor/build-support/`
are copied from Myna at commit

    99eba4370ffea3b0d3ab9f1c9edefc53a8bb798d   (2026-10-19)

into this repository, because the floating capsule's layout had to be
changed (see below) and the renderer is a separate program we ship
sources for. Each vendored file keeps its original contents apart from the
modifications listed here:

  1. `myna-hud/src/pill.rs`
     - `LABEL_MAX_CHARS: i32 = 30` replaced by `LABEL_MAX_WIDTH: i32 = 420`
       (pixels) plus `LABEL_MIN_WIDTH`. The old constant was handed to
       `GtkLabel::set_max_width_chars`, whose unit is Pango's *average Latin
       character width* — keeping a status on one line by that measure is
       not possible for CJK text.
     - The status label no longer wraps (`set_wrap(false)` +
       `set_single_line_mode(true)`) and sits inside a `GtkScrolledWindow`
       capped at `LABEL_MAX_WIDTH`, so it stays one line while the pill
       widens and then scrolls.
     - `scroll_label_to_end()` added: parks the horizontal adjustment at its
       maximum after each status change, so the newest words stay visible
       and the oldest scroll off to the left.
     - `label_max_width()` / `fixed_chrome_width()` accessors added for the
       window's sizing.
     - `PILL_HEIGHT` raised 58 -> 60, the measured content height with the
       label viewport in place, so the pill does not grow 2px on the first
       status.
  2. `myna-hud/src/window.rs`
     - `fit_size()` caps the window width at
       `fixed_chrome_width() + label_max_width()`. A `GtkScrolledWindow`
       reports its child's width as its *minimum*, which
       `set_max_content_width` does not clamp, so the cap has to be applied
       here.
  3. `myna-hud/src/style.css`
     - `.myna-hud-label-view` rule added, making the viewport invisible (no
       frame, background or overshoot indicator).
  4. `vendor/Cargo.toml` is not upstream's: it is a small workspace manifest
     listing the two vendored crates, so the tree builds standalone with
     `cargo build -p myna-hud` and needs no external checkout.
  5. `vendor/myna-hud/examples/scroll_check.rs` is new work for this
     project: a graphical self-check that the capsule stays one line at a
     constant height, stops widening at `LABEL_MAX_WIDTH` and scrolls to the
     end.
  6. Tests, docs and unrelated modules are vendored unmodified.

`vendor/.version` is generated at packaging time (`debian/rules`) from
`debian/changelog`; upstream resolves it from git or a staged file.

Build: `scripts/build-myna-hud.sh` compiles `vendor/` and installs the
binary to `~/.local/bin/myna-hud`. Passing `MYNA_SOURCE_DIR=/path/to/myna`
builds an *unmodified* upstream tree instead (the capsule then wraps).

### Not vendored

  - The application icon (`src/doubao_input/resources/logo.svg`, installed
    as `doubao-input.svg`) is Myna's icon
    (`client/data/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/com.canonical.Myna.svg`), used
    unmodified.
  - The GNOME Shell overlay host is **not** distributed here: an installed
    `myna-shell@canonical.com` extension (from Myna's own tree, installed by
    `scripts/install-gnome-extension.sh`) hosts the renderer's window when
    present. Without it the renderer presents as an ordinary window.
  - The settings window (`src/doubao_input/ui/control_window.py`) is original
    code written in Myna Settings' libadwaita style
    (Adw.ApplicationWindow / ToolbarView / ViewStack / PreferencesPage); it
    is a re-implementation of the look, not a copy of Myna's source.

Because both projects are AGPL-3.0-or-later, the vendored sources are
redistributed here under the same terms (see `LICENSE`).
